WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.278
Scheduling books appointments with the people, rooms and equipment of your business, and

00:00:06.278 --> 00:00:09.029
offers only the times that are really free.

00:00:09.029 --> 00:00:13.240
This video shows how to add the people, rooms and equipment that take

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.890
appointments, and how to describe each kind of appointment.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:25.330
A clinic, a studio or a service team has the same problem.

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.830
Customers want a time, and that time depends on who is working, which

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.650
room is free, and what is already booked.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.983
Scheduling answers it with two things you set up once.

00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:41.462
Resources are the people, rooms and equipment that take appointments.

00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:46.120
Appointment types describe each kind of appointment and who can take it.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.299
With both in place, the site offers only times that are really free,

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:54.890
and the same person or room can never be booked twice.

00:00:59.073 --> 00:01:02.201
Open Calendars, Scheduling Resources.

00:01:02.201 --> 00:01:05.693
The list is empty, so choose Add resource.

00:01:06.144 --> 00:01:07.768
Start with a person.

00:01:07.768 --> 00:01:09.267
Type the name, Dr.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:12.515
Maya Chen, and leave the kind on Staff member.

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:15.764
The other kinds are Room, Equipment and Other.

00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:19.114
For a staff member, choose the user they are.

00:01:19.114 --> 00:01:23.715
Their own calendars then count too, so a meeting on their personal calendar

00:01:23.715 --> 00:01:25.987
keeps that time from being booked.

00:01:26.437 --> 00:01:28.761
Calendar is where appointments go.

00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:33.351
Leave it on Make a new calendar and the site creates one for this person.

00:01:33.351 --> 00:01:36.430
Time zone is the zone the working hours are in.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:41.077
Untick Takes appointments to stop offering a resource without deleting it.

00:01:41.529 --> 00:01:43.981
Working hours take one line per day.

00:01:43.981 --> 00:01:47.659
Two ranges on a line leave a gap, here a lunch break, and

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:50.169
a day that isn't listed is a day off.

00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:53.821
Days off and changed days take one line each:

00:01:53.821 --> 00:01:56.894
a closed day, or shorter hours on one date.

00:01:56.894 --> 00:02:03.103
Hours can also come from shifts on a calendar, which suits staff who are scheduled elsewhere.

00:02:03.103 --> 00:02:04.232
Choose Save.

00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:07.546
Rooms and equipment are resources too.

00:02:07.546 --> 00:02:10.604
Add Treatment room 1, with the kind Room.

00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:14.573
It has no user, and its hours are written the same way.

00:02:15.023 --> 00:02:17.593
Each resource appears in the list.

00:02:17.593 --> 00:02:21.383
Deleting one keeps its calendar and its appointments.

00:02:25.587 --> 00:02:30.005
Open Calendars, Appointment Types and choose Add appointment type.

00:02:30.005 --> 00:02:32.950
The General card holds what customers see:

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:37.491
the Name, a Description, the Location, a Color for its events on the

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:39.577
calendar, and Can be booked.

00:02:40.028 --> 00:02:44.070
The Time card sets the Length of an appointment, and how far apart

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.979
the offered start times are.

00:02:45.979 --> 00:02:50.694
Free time before and after is time the resource needs around each appointment,

00:02:50.694 --> 00:02:52.154
such as cleaning up.

00:02:52.154 --> 00:02:54.118
Other plans can't fall in it.

00:02:54.571 --> 00:02:58.127
Under Who, choose the Resources that take this appointment.

00:02:58.127 --> 00:02:59.824
Pick decides who gets it.

00:02:59.824 --> 00:03:03.708
Any free resource takes the first one that is free, and Share out

00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:07.101
gives it to the one with the fewest recent appointments.

00:03:07.556 --> 00:03:12.988
All resources together needs every resource at once, such as a doctor and a room.

00:03:12.988 --> 00:03:18.046
Places per appointment above one makes a class that several customers book.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:23.162
Booking rules set the minimum notice, how many days ahead customers can book,

00:03:23.162 --> 00:03:27.207
the most appointments per resource per day, and how long a time is

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.678
held for someone who is still booking.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:34.573
Tick Bookings wait for someone to confirm them to review requests first.

00:03:34.573 --> 00:03:39.016
Customers can book it themselves puts the type on a public booking page,

00:03:39.016 --> 00:03:40.725
at the address you type.

00:03:40.725 --> 00:03:41.750
Choose Save.

00:03:42.201 --> 00:03:45.853
The type appears in the list, with a Book button for booking it.

00:03:45.853 --> 00:03:48.201
Deleting a type keeps its appointments.

00:03:52.396 --> 00:03:56.543
Every resource has its own calendar, of the Appointments type.

00:03:56.543 --> 00:04:00.202
Open Calendars, Calendar, and tick the calendar of Dr.

00:04:00.202 --> 00:04:03.556
Maya Chen or of the room to see its appointments.

00:04:04.008 --> 00:04:08.081
Anything you add to that calendar, such as a Blocked time event, keeps

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.904
that time from being booked.

00:04:09.904 --> 00:04:13.388
The next video shows exactly how open times are worked out.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:20.003
Resources say who and what can take appointments, and appointment types say how

00:04:20.003 --> 00:04:22.446
long they last and how they are booked.

00:04:22.446 --> 00:04:23.858
Thanks for watching.

